-- 025_nanp_prefixes — per-NPA longest-prefix rows so +1 resolves by area code.
-- Root cause of the +1→Canada bug: no prefix rows exist for NANP, so
-- resolveCountry() fell through to the calling_code fallback, where
-- `WHERE digits LIKE calling_code || '%'` matches BOTH Canada ('1') and USA
-- ('1') and the row order picked Canada every time. With these rows the
-- longest-prefix match wins first (1416 → Canada, 1212 → USA) and the
-- engine's classifyNanp() guard covers any NPA missing here.
-- Idempotent: UNIQUE(prefix, operator) with NULL operator — re-runs skip.
